# Project-root guard.
#
# Two purposes:
#   1. When the web host serves files from above /public/ (common on shared
#      hosting where the user cannot reassign DocumentRoot), redirect all
#      traffic to /public/ so nothing else leaks.
#   2. Defence-in-depth: block direct access to dotfiles, the .env file, and
#      every server-side folder. Even if rewrites are disabled, these rules
#      ensure config and source code are unreadable from the browser.

# --- 1. Convenience redirect ------------------------------------------------
# When a host's DocumentRoot points at this project (rather than at /public/),
# the bare URL is handled by a tiny index.php at the project root that issues
# a 302 to /public/. The .htaccess rules below only enforce security.

# --- 2. Deny direct access to dotfiles, .env, and source folders ------------
<FilesMatch "^\.">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

<Files ".env">
    Require all denied
</Files>
<Files ".env.example">
    Require all denied
</Files>
<Files "composer.json">
    Require all denied
</Files>
<Files "composer.lock">
    Require all denied
</Files>
<Files "*.sqlite">
    Require all denied
</Files>
<Files "*.sqlite-journal">
    Require all denied
</Files>
<Files "*.sqlite-wal">
    Require all denied
</Files>
<Files "*.sqlite-shm">
    Require all denied
</Files>
<Files "*.xlsx">
    Require all denied
</Files>
<Files "*.bak">
    Require all denied
</Files>

# Block directory listing.
Options -Indexes
